{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'curl -fsSL https://qrypt-quickstart.pages.dev/'","aggregated_output":"<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><title>Qrypt quantum entropy quickstart: AES-256 key in 5 minutes</title><meta name=\"description\" content=\"Get an AES-256-GCM key from Qrypt quantum entropy in about 5 minutes with Python or Node.\"><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/style.css\"><link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/highlight.css\"></head><body>\n<a class=\"skip\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a><header><nav aria-label=\"Site\"><a href=\"/\">Quickstart</a><a href=\"/troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</a><a href=\"/llms.txt\">llms.txt</a></nav></header><main id=\"main\">\n<h1>Make an AES-256 key from quantum entropy</h1>\n<aside class=\"agent-note\" aria-label=\"Note for AI coding agents\"><p><strong>AI coding agents, read this first:</strong> if a <code>.env</code> file already exists, do not open or print it in any way (no <code>cat</code>, <code>head</code>, <code>sed</code> or <code>ls</code> of its contents). Check it only with <code>grep -q '^QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED] .env &amp;&amp; echo set</code>. If <code>.env</code> says <em>Permission denied</em>, you are in the Qrypt agent sandbox on purpose: do not try to read it, and run your program with <code>qrypt-run quickstart.py</code> (or <code>qrypt-run quickstart.mjs</code>). Create the project files in the current directory, next to <code>.env</code>. Do not make a subfolder or copy <code>.env</code>. Machine-readable version: <a href=\"/llms.txt\">/llms.txt</a>.</p></aside>\n\n<p><span class=\"time\">Time target: about 5 minutes</span> No SDK needed: one HTTPS GET, then standard crypto.</p>\n<h2>1. Get a token</h2>\n<p>Create an account at <a href=\"https://portal.qrypt.com/register\">portal.qrypt.com/register</a> and generate a token for the <strong>Entropy</strong> service. It is shown only once and is billed like a password: keep it secret.</p>\n<h2>2. Save it in <code>.env</code></h2>\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-env\" aria-label=\"Copy .env line\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-env\" data-lang=\"env\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nv\">QRYPT_API_KEY</span><span class=\"o\">=</span>paste-your-token-here</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Put <code>.env</code> next to the script and add it to <code>.gitignore</code>. Never print it, not even partly (no <code>cat .env</code>). To check it is set, run <code>grep -q '^QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED] .env &amp;&amp; echo set</code>.</p>\n<h2>3. Run the snippet</h2>\n<div role=\"tablist\" aria-label=\"Language\">\n<button role=\"tab\" id=\"t-py\" aria-selected=\"true\" aria-controls=\"p-py\">Python</button>\n<button role=\"tab\" id=\"t-js\" aria-selected=\"false\" aria-controls=\"p-js\" tabindex=\"-1\">Node</button></div>\n<section role=\"tabpanel\" id=\"p-py\" aria-labelledby=\"t-py\" tabindex=\"0\">\n<p>Python 3.9+. Uses <code>requests</code>: Cloudflare blocks Python's built-in <code>urllib</code> User-Agent.</p>\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-pyi\" aria-label=\"Copy Python install command\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-pyi\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"line\">python3<span class=\"w\"> </span>-m<span class=\"w\"> </span>venv<span class=\"w\"> </span>.venv<span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;&amp;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span>.venv/bin/pip<span class=\"w\"> </span>install<span class=\"w\"> </span>requests<span class=\"w\"> </span>cryptography<span class=\"w\"> </span>python-dotenv</span></code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-py\" aria-label=\"Copy Python quickstart code\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-py\" data-lang=\"python\" class=\"numbered\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Qrypt quickstart (Python): 1 KiB of quantum entropy -&gt; AES-256-GCM key.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Setup: pip install requests cryptography python-dotenv</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Then put QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED] token&gt; in a .env file next to this script.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">base64</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">os</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">sys</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">requests</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">cryptography.hazmat.primitives.ciphers.aead</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">AESGCM</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kn\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nn\">dotenv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span> <span class=\"n\">load_dotenv</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">API</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getenv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;QRYPT_BASE_URL&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;https://api-eus.qrypt.com&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>  <span class=\"c1\"># mock override</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># One friendly message per failure. We never retry automatically.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">HELP</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;QRYPT_API_KEY is missing: add it to .env (see .env.example).&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"mi\">400</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;400: size must be 1-512. It counts KiB, not bytes.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"mi\">401</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;401: Authorization header missing, malformed or expired.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"mi\">403</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;403: Token invalid OR monthly quota used. Check the token first.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"mi\">429</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;429: rate limited. Live can return 429 about 1 s after a single &quot;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">             <span class=\"s2\">&quot;prior call; wait 10 s or more and never loop.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># 500, 503 and anything else: Qrypt is busy or erroring, so try again later.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Step 1: read the token from .env. Never print or log it.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">load_dotenv</span><span class=\"p\">()</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">token</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getenv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;QRYPT_API_KEY&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"ow\">or</span> <span class=\"n\">sys</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">exit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HELP</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">])</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Step 2: fetch 1 KiB of entropy. A custom User-Agent avoids Cloudflare&#39;s</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># block on Python&#39;s urllib; X-Qrypt-Client tags quickstart traffic.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">headers</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"p\">{</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"s2\">&quot;Authorization&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Bearer </span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">token</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;Accept&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;application/json&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"s2\">&quot;User-Agent&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;qrypt-quickstart/1.0&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;X-Qrypt-Client&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"s2\">&quot;quickstart-py/1.0&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">try</span><span class=\"p\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"n\">resp</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">requests</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">API</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">/api/v1/quantum-entropy&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">params</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;size&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span> <span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"p\">},</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">                        <span class=\"n\">headers</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">headers</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">timeout</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mi\">15</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"k\">if</span> <span class=\"n\">resp</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">status_code</span> <span class=\"o\">!=</span> <span class=\"mi\">200</span><span class=\"p\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"n\">sys</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">exit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HELP</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">get</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">resp</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">status_code</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"sa\">f</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;</span><span class=\"si\">{</span><span class=\"n\">resp</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">status_code</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"s2\">: Qrypt is &quot;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">                          <span class=\"s2\">&quot;busy or erroring. Try again shortly.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"n\">entropy_b64</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">resp</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">json</span><span class=\"p\">()[</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;random&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">][</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"p\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">except</span> <span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">requests</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">RequestException</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"ne\">ValueError</span><span class=\"p\">):</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"n\">sys</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">exit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Network error or non-JSON reply: check proxy/TLS, retry soon.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Step 3: decode first, then keep 32 bytes as the AES-256 key.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">key</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">base64</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">b64decode</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">entropy_b64</span><span class=\"p\">)[:</span><span class=\"mi\">32</span><span class=\"p\">]</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\"># Step 4: encrypt and decrypt a sample message with AES-256-GCM.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"n\">aes</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">nonce</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">message</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">AESGCM</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">key</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"n\">os</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">urandom</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">12</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"sa\">b</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;hello, quantum entropy&quot;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">assert</span> <span class=\"n\">aes</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">decrypt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nonce</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">aes</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">encrypt</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">nonce</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">message</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">),</span> <span class=\"kc\">None</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"o\">==</span> <span class=\"n\">message</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nb\">print</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Success: AES-256-GCM round trip with a Qrypt key (not shown).&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span></span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-pyr\" aria-label=\"Copy Python run command\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-pyr\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"line\">.venv/bin/python<span class=\"w\"> </span>quickstart.py</span></code></pre></div></section>\n<section role=\"tabpanel\" id=\"p-js\" aria-labelledby=\"t-js\" tabindex=\"0\" hidden>\n<p>Node 20.12+ (built-in <code>fetch</code> and <code>process.loadEnvFile</code>). No dependencies.</p>\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-js\" aria-label=\"Copy Node quickstart code\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-js\" data-lang=\"js\" class=\"numbered\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// Qrypt quickstart (Node 20.12+): 1 KiB of quantum entropy -&gt; AES-256-GCM key.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// No dependencies. Put QRYPT_API_KEY=[REDACTED] token&gt; in a .env file here.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">assert</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kr\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;node:assert&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">existsSync</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kr\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;node:fs&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">createCipheriv</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">createDecipheriv</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">randomBytes</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kr\">from</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;node:crypto&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">API</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">process</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">env</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">QRYPT_BASE_URL</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">??</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;https://api-eus.qrypt.com&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">// mock</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// One friendly message per failure. We never retry automatically.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">HELP</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">missing</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;QRYPT_API_KEY is missing: add it to .env.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nx\">network</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Network error or non-JSON reply: check proxy/TLS, retry soon.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mf\">400</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;400: size must be 1-512. It counts KiB, not bytes.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mf\">401</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;401: Authorization header missing, malformed or expired.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mf\">403</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;403: Token invalid OR monthly quota used. Check the token first.&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mf\">429</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;429: rate limited. Live can return 429 about 1 s after a single &quot;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;prior call; wait 10 s or more and never loop.&quot;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">};</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// 500, 503 and anything else: Qrypt is busy or erroring, so try again later.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fail</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">msg</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">error</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">msg</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">process</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">exit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">1</span><span class=\"p\">);</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">};</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// Step 1: read the token from .env. Never print or log it.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">existsSync</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;.env&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">process</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">loadEnvFile</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;.env&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">token</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">process</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">env</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">QRYPT_API_KEY</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">||</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fail</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">HELP</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">missing</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// Step 2: fetch 1 KiB of entropy (size counts KiB, not bytes).</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">headers</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Authorization</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sb\">`Bearer </span><span class=\"si\">${</span><span class=\"nx\">token</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"sb\">`</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Accept</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;application/json&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;User-Agent&quot;</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;qrypt-quickstart/1.0&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;X-Qrypt-Client&quot;</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;quickstart-js/1.0&quot;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">};</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">url</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"sb\">`</span><span class=\"si\">${</span><span class=\"nx\">API</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"sb\">/api/v1/quantum-entropy?size=1`</span><span class=\"p\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">await</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fetch</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">url</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">headers</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">}).</span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"p\">(()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fail</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">HELP</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">network</span><span class=\"p\">));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">status</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">!==</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">200</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fail</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">HELP</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">status</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">??</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sb\">`</span><span class=\"si\">${</span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">status</span><span class=\"si\">}</span><span class=\"sb\">: Qrypt is busy or erroring. Try again shortly.`</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">body</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">await</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">res</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">json</span><span class=\"p\">().</span><span class=\"k\">catch</span><span class=\"p\">(()</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">fail</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">HELP</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">network</span><span class=\"p\">));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// Step 3: decode first, then keep 32 bytes as the AES-256 key.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">key</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Buffer</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kr\">from</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">body</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">random</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">0</span><span class=\"p\">],</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;base64&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"nx\">subarray</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">32</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"c1\">// Step 4: encrypt and decrypt a sample message with AES-256-GCM.</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">GCM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;aes-256-gcm&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">iv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">randomBytes</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">12</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">message</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;hello, quantum&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">enc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">createCipheriv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">GCM</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">key</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">iv</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">sealed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Buffer</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">concat</span><span class=\"p\">([</span><span class=\"nx\">enc</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">update</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">message</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;utf8&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">enc</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kr\">final</span><span class=\"p\">()]);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"kd\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">dec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">createDecipheriv</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">GCM</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">key</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">iv</span><span class=\"p\">).</span><span class=\"nx\">setAuthTag</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">enc</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">getAuthTag</span><span class=\"p\">());</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nx\">assert</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">equal</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">dec</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">update</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">sealed</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kc\">null</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;utf8&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">dec</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"kr\">final</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;utf8&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">message</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"nx\">console</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">log</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;Success: AES-256-GCM round trip with a Qrypt key (not shown).&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">);</span></span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-jsr\" aria-label=\"Copy Node run command\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-jsr\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"line\">node<span class=\"w\"> </span>quickstart.mjs</span></code></pre></div></section>\n<h2>What the API returns</h2>\n<p>One base64 string per KiB requested. Decode it before use; it never contains the key itself.</p>\n<pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code data-lang=\"json\"><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"p\">{</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nt\">&quot;random&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">&quot;&lt;base64 string: 1,024 random bytes when decoded&gt;&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">],</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"nt\">&quot;size&quot;</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span class=\"p\">}</span></span></code></pre>\n<h2>4. Expected output</h2>\n<pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code data-lang=\"text\"><span class=\"line\">Success: AES-256-GCM round trip with a Qrypt entropy key (key not shown).</span></code></pre>\n<h2>Things that trip people up</h2>\n<ul><li><code>size</code> counts <strong>KiB</strong>, not bytes. Ask for <code>size=1</code> (1,024 bytes) and take 32 bytes.</li>\n<li>Base64-decode the string first; never use the text itself as the key.</li>\n<li>Live can return 429 about 1 s after a single prior call; wait 10 s or more and never loop.</li>\n<li>A wrong token returns <strong>403</strong>, the same as an exhausted quota. Check the token first.</li>\n<li>Never print, log or commit the key or token. Use fresh entropy for each key.</li></ul>\n<p>Errors? See <a href=\"/troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</a>.</p>\n<section aria-labelledby=\"h-agent\"><h2 id=\"h-agent\">Using an AI coding agent?</h2>\n<p>In our tests, AI agents read part of <code>.env</code> (for example <code>head -c 20 .env</code>) in 14 of 15 runs, even when these docs told them not to. A doc can't stop that habit, but file permissions can. Run your agent inside this small Docker sandbox:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Download the sandbox files: <a href=\"/agent-sandbox/Dockerfile\">Dockerfile</a>, <a href=\"/agent-sandbox/entrypoint.sh\">entrypoint.sh</a>, <a href=\"/agent-sandbox/qrypt-run\">qrypt-run</a>, <a href=\"/agent-sandbox/qrypt-run-inner\">qrypt-run-inner</a>, <a href=\"/agent-sandbox/run.sh\">run.sh</a>, all into one folder called <code>agent-sandbox/</code>. Then run <code>chmod +x agent-sandbox/*.sh agent-sandbox/qrypt-run*</code>.</li>\n<li>Start the agent inside it (the project folder must already contain your <code>.env</code>):\n<div class=\"codebox\"><button class=\"copy\" data-target=\"c-sbx\" aria-label=\"Copy sandbox start command\">Copy</button><pre class=\"hl\" tabindex=\"0\"><code id=\"c-sbx\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"line\">agent-sandbox/run.sh<span class=\"w\"> </span>~/my-project<span class=\"w\"> </span>~/my-project/.env<span class=\"w\"> </span>your-agent-command</span></code></pre></div></li>\n<li>Inside the sandbox, the agent runs as user <code>agent</code>. <code>.env</code> belongs to a separate user (<code>qrypt</code>, mode 600), so <code>cat .env</code> gets <em>Permission denied</em>. The program runs with <code>qrypt-run quickstart.py</code>, a fixed rule that runs one <code>.py</code>/<code>.mjs</code>/<code>.js</code> file as the <code>qrypt</code> user, so it can still read <code>QRYPT_API_KEY</code> from <code>.env</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>The agent CLI has to be available in the container. Either add it to the Dockerfile (for example <code>RUN npm i -g your-agent</code>) or mount it by setting <code>SANDBOX_DOCKER_ARGS</code>. For example, for Cursor CLI: <code>SANDBOX_DOCKER_ARGS=\"-v $HOME/.local/share/cursor-agent/versions/VERSION:/opt/cursor-agent:ro -v $HOME/agent-home:/home/agent -e PATH=/opt/cursor-agent:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin\"</code>, with your agent's login file copied into <code>~/agent-home</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Limits:</strong> this stops accidental reads such as <code>cat</code>, <code>head</code> or an editor opening <code>.env</code>. It does not stop an agent that deliberately writes a program to print the token and runs it with <code>qrypt-run</code>. Review what your agent runs, and use a test token, not a production one.</p>\n</section>\n<p id=\"copy-status\" class=\"sr\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p></main><footer><p>Unofficial quickstart. API reference: <a href=\"https://docs.qrypt.com/eaas/\">docs.qrypt.com/eaas</a>. No analytics or cookies.</p></footer>\n<script src=\"/app.js\" defer></script></body></html>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
